Update the NGO web application to add a new Vidya Jyothi menu item and implement a Vidyanjali Education Requirement Generation module.
Objective
Create a web page that automates the existing Excel-based workflow from:
Vidyanjali_School_Adoption_Budget_Tool_v1.xlsx
KaghazNagar-Schools-list.xlsx
The feature should allow NGO staff or school staff to select a district, mandal/block, and school, review school details, select required work areas and components, enter units/quantities, automatically calculate estimated budget, and generate a school requirement/proposal planning output.
Navigation
Add a new main menu item:
Vidya Jyothi
When clicked, it should open:
Vidyanjali – Education Requirement Generation
Suggested route:
/vidya-jyothi/vidyanjali-requirements
Data Source Requirements
Use the Excel data as the master input.
School Data
Load school data from:
KaghazNagar-Schools-list.xlsx
The application should support filtering schools by:
State
District
Mandal / Block
UDISE Code
School Name
Address
Status
Example school record to support:
UDISE Code: 36021100201
Active Status: Operational
Academic Year: 2026-27
State: TELANGANA
District: KUMURAM BHEEM ASIFABAD
Block: KOUTHALA
School Name: MPPS SANDGAON
Address: sandgaon, KOUTHALA, KOMARAM BHEEM
Show active/operational status in green.
Budget Tool Data
Load work areas, sub-components, items, unit types, estimated costs, and any available remarks from:
Vidyanjali_School_Adoption_Budget_Tool_v1.xlsx
All Excel sheet columns should be represented in the application wherever applicable.
Do not hard-code only one school or one block. Build the import logic so the page dynamically loads available data from the Excel-derived dataset.
