Print
Functional Requirements
Add Vidya Jyothi menu item.
Create Vidyanjali requirement generation page.
Load school data from Excel-derived data source.
Load work areas and budget items from Excel-derived data source.
District selection should filter mandals/blocks.
Mandal/block selection should filter schools.
School grid should show UDISE, school name, address, district, block, and status.
User should be able to select a school.
User should be able to select work areas and budget items.
User should be able to enter quantity/units for each selected item.
Estimated amount should calculate automatically.
Total budget should update dynamically.
Generate final school requirement/proposal output.
Save generated requirement/proposal.
Support export or print output if existing app has export framework.
Keep UI simple and staff-friendly.
Import / Seed Requirement
Add a script or service to import the Excel files into the application database or JSON data store.
The importer should:
Read all sheets from the budget tool workbook.
Preserve column names as much as possible.
Normalize work areas, components, sub-components, item names, unit types, and costs.
Read all schools from the school list workbook.
Normalize district, block/mandal, UDISE code, school name, address, and status.
Avoid duplicate school records by UDISE code.
Avoid duplicate budget items by work area + component + item name.
If the current application does not have database support, create structured JSON files under a data folder such as:
/data/vidyanjali/schools.json
/data/vidyanjali/workAreas.json
/data/vidyanjali/components.json
Validation Rules
School selection is required before proposal generation.
Quantity must be a positive number for selected items.
Unit cost must be numeric.
Estimated start date is optional but should be included in final output if entered.
Do not allow proposal generation with zero selected items.
Show clear error messages for missing school, missing quantity, or invalid cost.
